nadmitted LOCAL root/prefix must refuse before LOCAL entry bodies; a later selected root must refuse before ITS dependent payloads and before any completed inventory. Local entry planning after actual local-entry admission is not permission to read the yet-unadmitted retained/custom payload. Do not claim zero local-entry reads for a failure discovered only by that planning; claim and witness the actual boundary.\n\nRequired distinguishing witnesses in later Source: forbidden local metadata at the final prefix position gives zero local-entry/dependency payload reads; admitted local entries selecting an uncovered/custom additional root at the final position/node may be planned but give zero rule/snapshot/value/custom/foreign/text payload reads and no manifest; ordinary covered dependency case completes; prefix/body identity or cutoff drift refuses; phase-boundary byte/call/node/attempt/deadline exhaustion cannot reset/top-up or finish late. Existing canonical/hash/support/frame claims and all8consumer completeness remain subject to exact Source review and the once-frozen gate.\n\nI inspected only the named archive-prefix.ts, archive-privacy.ts, retained-plan.ts, archive-budget.ts and policy interfaces at8a0181994 to answer ordering. Their current names/comments or green partial witnesses do not prove these boundaries; this checkpoint is ungated/not formally reviewed. No broad implementation acceptance, export eligibility/configuration, provider/push/deployment action or test/gate run follows from this advice.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4b4134f6131038810e97d63637d91a4783e11114","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:34ce1438541d63ecba2e5d29b68b8f5b12a14964"}}